    "body": "@smaug---- sorry I was trying to simplify my actual code to make it more readable here. I'll clean it up.\n\nThe point is that in order to safely use `moveBefore()` we have to reimplement the checks that it does and fall back to `insertBefore()` if our nodes don't meet the requirements. It would be a lot easier, and likely faster, if there was a DOM API that just did this for us. I don't see the benefit in forcing this conditional logic to be wrapped around so many `moveBefore() calls.",
