    "created_at": "2026-10-28T15:02:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T15:02:00Z",
    "body": "It seems like the developer sentiment here is basically \"I always want to move an element if I can and fallback to insert if I must,\" and the claim would be that you want to move an element 100% of the time if you can and therefore this API that makes that hard is cumbersome.\n\nBased on the [previous](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1406#issuecomment-5739681021) [comments](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1406#issuecomment-5761593936) from @annevk and @smaug----, it seems like this may not be a viewpoint shared by implementors. So I think it's fair to ask, can you give a practical example of when it would make sense *not* to move an element if you can?",
