    "created_at": "2026-11-01T21:12:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-01T21:12:46Z",
    "body": "I'm struggling to see why there is compat risk in changing the moving conditions that back `moveOrInsertBefore()`, but no equivalent compat risk changing those same conditions that back `moveBefore()`? In both cases, the developer is specifying clear intent (one is more general than the other of course).\n\nI guess @annevk is saying that the intent with `moveOrInsertBefore()` is muddier, and that the behavior change that `moveBefore()` would experience (`thrown error => successful move`) is simpler / less error-prone compared to the behavior change that `moveOrInsertBefore()` would experience (`successful insert => successful move`)? @annevk is that your argument?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
